{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Every leper and every zav and everyone impure through a corpse.</b> These are of seven-day impurity and they render others impure; therefore one who had a seminal emission does not go outside the camp, and there is no hand [privy] in the camp to go outside, but rather each one digs in his tent, as is the practice of all camps, for there are infants among them. And the section 'When you go out as a camp' (Deuteronomy 23:10–15) speaks of a small camp in which there is no woman, and the Ark is among them, and they are not surrounded [in the same way], for in the camp of Israel the Shekhinah is in the middle. And I will further explain it in its place."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "Resolved והם / סובבים variant: adopted סובבים ('surrounded') per the translation; the alternate reading והם ('and they') appears in some witnesses."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:16:24.065794702Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}